00:00:00.560 --> 00:00:02.869 align:start position:0%
 
over the past decade none of batman's  growing family of friends have proven  quite so exciting as batwoman  especially now that she has finally made  her small screen debut  but just who is batwoman here's a look  at the untold truth behind one of dc's  most  fascinating characters kathy kane the  original batwoman debuted in detective  comics number 233  in july 1956. unfortunately the  character wasn't introduced by dc  out of any real desire to expand  batman's universe  instead kathy kane was concocted to  combat some scurrilous rumors  about the caped crusader in 1954  the psychiatrist frederick wortham had  published seduction of the innocent  a highly dubious yet influential  treatise on the dangers of superhero  comics  in this book wertham had this to say  about batman and robin's relationship  it is like a wish dream of two  homosexuals living together  holy romeo and juliet wertham's book  would go on to spark  full-blown congressional hearings and  devastate the world of genre fiction  and while most superhero titles escaped  unscathed  batman's editors decided that they  needed to restore the appearance of  heteronormativity to gotham city  thus kathy kane the batwoman as a  wealthy socialite and former circus  performer whose admiration for batman  drove her to a life of crime fighting  kathy was a love interest in the style  of superman's ever popular lois lane  of course bruce wayne has a thing for  her but she only has eyes for batman  and to complicate matters he knows her  secret identity but  she doesn't know his this dynamic  produced some fairly interesting early  adventures and  even introduced a sidekick in the form  of cathy's niece betty  the original batgirl who was a similarly  positioned  love interest for robin in the end  though kathy proved to be more popular  with readers than she was with incoming  batman editor  julius schwartz who pared down the  batman family dramatically when he took  over  in the early 60s while kathy kane was  eventually phased out of the comics the  idea of keeping a woman in the batman  family persisted elsewhere  specifically on television in 1967  at the height of the batman tv show's  popularity the producers decided to  expand their cast  and introduce a new batgirl glad to have  you flanking this bad girl  the tv show tied the new batgirl to an  existing character by introducing her as  barbara gordon  the daughter of gotham city's solemn and  stentorian police commissioner the  viewers were clued in on her secret  identity but  unlike kathy kane batman and robin  initially had no idea who she really was  batgirl proved to be a reliably popular  member of the tv show's bat  family and soon enough barbara gordon  was introduced in the comics too the  comic book version of barbara was just  as popular with fans as her tv  counterpart  as a result the character served as  batgirl until 1988  and then stepped back into the role from  2011 to the present  even when she wasn't batgirl barbara  regularly featured as  oracle an incredibly skilled hacker who  often provided vital information to  batman  and the justice league when batman  family launched in 1975  the second issue asked readers to write  in with their picks for which secondary  batman characters they wanted to see  featured alongside batgirl and robin  apparently the response was strong  enough that they featured a reprint of  an early batwoman story in the next  issue  by then the fan letters were demanding a  proper comeback for kathy kane in number  10  these readers finally got their wish  when batwoman came out of retirement for  a team-up story with her successor  batgirl at the end of the story kathy  offers barbara the title of batwoman  babs refuses however claiming that while  it was an honor  there can be only one batwoman soon  enough though  there'd be no bat women at all four  years later  in detective comics number 485 that  woman is killed  by the league of assassins that was the  last reader saw of the main universe's  kathy kane for nearly 30 years  and in the mid-80s crisis on infinite  earths rearranged the timeline so that  she never existed  at all in 1999 barbara gordon was busy  being oracle  and kathy kane had been written out of  existence so there was nothing stopping  dc from teasing a potential new female  bat character  in the pages of the no man's land story  arc no man's land follows the heroes and  villains of gotham in the aftermath of a  devastating earthquake which leaves the  entire city as little more than a  post-apocalyptic ruin  all but abandoned by the us government  gotham becomes a battleground for the  countless gangs and supervillains who  are vying for domination  what's worse batman has been missing for  three months  so naturally someone puts on a bat  costume and starts claiming territory in  his name  this particular batwoman turns out to be  the huntress but she  isn't the only one to wear the  distinctive costume during no man's land  at the end of the story the cowl is  passed on to cassandra kane  a teenager who is trained since birth to  become an assassin  with the huntress back in her normal  identity cassandra decides to become the  new batgirl  leaving the door open for an all-new  batwoman to appear  in 2006 the dc universe jumped forward  by a year  and then explained everything in a  year-long weekly mini-series called 52.  the series set the stage for plenty of  major developments  the most prominent and long-lasting of  which was the introduction of the  all-new batwoman  kate kane not to be confused with the  silver ages kathy kane  kate sported a brand new black and red  costume designed by alex ross  she also made headlines after she was  introduced as dc's highest profile  lesbian character  especially once she took over detective  comics as its headlining star  while kate used batman's iconography in  order to strike fear into gotham city's  criminals  she was dramatically different from the  caped crusader she had military training  was significantly less averse to  firearms and her equivalent to alfred  was her father  a retired general who provided her with  the experimental military hardware  there was however one key similarity  between kate  and bruce she too was driven to fight  crime after seeing her family killed in  front of her  in this case her mother and twin sister  detective comics number 858 dives into  kate kane's origin story  and the following issue deals with her  dismissal from the united states  military academy during her senior year  while training at west point kate is  accused of being in violation of article  125  of the uniform military code of justice  just in case you're not totally up to  speed on the specifics of military law  that's the article concerning  homosexuality which was once used  to keep lgbtq people out of the military  while kate is offered the chance to  claim that it was  all a misunderstanding she instead  chooses to leave west point  and never fulfill her lifelong dream of  serving in the army  naturally that sense of integrity has  been one of her defining characteristics  ever since  it's worth noting that this story was  originally published in 2009  when the official policy of the military  was don't ask  don't tell meaning that gay people could  serve just as long as they were in the  closet  only two years later in 2011 that policy  was changed and article 125 was  officially repealed from the ucmj  that means that eventually kate's origin  may have to be retconned  however considering this would be a  fictional retcon that comes at the cost  of real world progress  it's no surprise that the creators of  that origin story  are absolutely fine with it when dc  rebooted their entire line in 2011 as  the new 52  batwoman got her first ongoing series  co-written by j.h williams iii  and william hayden blackman the most  notable addition to batwoman's roster  was maggie sawyer who first met kate  during her headlining run  in detective comics and quickly became  the character's love interest  maggie was originally introduced in the  superman books of the 90s  as a police officer in the metropolis  special crimes unit  back then she was one of the most  prominent gay characters in comics  playing a major role in superman's  ongoing saga in the early 2000s she was  transferred to gotham city's police  department in gotham central  a book that not coincidentally was  co-written by greg  raka one of kate's creators the  relationship between maggie and kate  became a huge part of the series  and led to a groundbreaking moment in  batwoman number 17  when kate proposes to maggie  unfortunately the marriage never came to  be  the editors at dc forbade the wedding  from taking place  a controversial decision that prompted  williams and blackman to walk out  in protest dc insisted that the decision  wasn't made as a result of an anti-lgbtq  agenda  but rather because of an editorial shift  that turned against marriage in  general with publisher dan de dio saying  that quote heroes shouldn't have happy  personal lives  but what what should we call you reign  miss parade  kane kate kane over the last decade  or so the cw has formed a full-on dc  multiverse on television with a core  roster featuring some of the most iconic  dc heroes  of all time occasionally the aeroverse  shows would cross over in massive  team-up events  one of these was the elseworlds story in  2018 which introduced a brand new  character to the arrowverse  batwoman as portrayed by ruby rose the  cw's take on batwoman exists in a gotham  city where batman disappeared  three years earlier leading to a surge  in crime and the need for a new  bat-themed vigilante crime fighter  in september 2019 the fully-fledged  batwoman series debuted with rose at the  forefront  and the cw ordered a second season just  a few weeks  later playing a major comic book  character on screen could be a career  defining move  for almost any actor and for a while it  looked like ruby rose would follow that  upward trajectory  however in may 2020 just a few months  after the cw asked for a second season  of batwoman  rose announced that she would be  departing the series in a statement she  said  this was not a decision i made lightly  as i have the utmost respect for the  cast  crew and everyone involved with the show  thank you to everyone who made season  one a success  i am truly grateful so why would an  actor walk away from a plum roll and a  regular gig on network television  variety later reported that rose had a  deep distaste for the series's long  shooting days which  led to tension on the set in the end a  mutual decision was made between rose  the cw  and warner brothers to find a new actor  to portray batwoman  in the same news reports announcing ruby  rose's exit from batwoman  the show's production company warner  brothers made it clear that this wasn't  going to spell the end for the series  within days of rose's departure it was  announced that kate kane would also be  cut from the show  in favor of a new character who uses the  batwoman alias  a leaked casting call revealed that  producers were looking for an actor  quote  female mid late 20s any ethnicity to  portray ryan wilder the new batwoman  who is supposed to be quote likable  messy a little goofy  and nothing like kate kane however  showrunner caroline dries  almost took the easier route of finding  a new actor to play kate  kane in an interview at the atx festival  at home  she explained i did consider the soap  opera version for a hot minute because  selfishly we already had a couple  episodes written  and transition wise it would be seamless  ultimately aeroverse overseer greg  berlanti made the decision to  introduce a new character along with a  fresh actor in the end  the new batwoman was revealed to be  javicia leslie  known for her roles on the bet crime  show the family business  and the cbs drama god friended me her  first appearance on batwoman came in a  january 2021 episode titled  appropriately enough whatever happened  to kate kane  check out one of our newest videos right  here plus  even more looper videos about your  favorite comics are coming soon  subscribe to our youtube channel and hit  the bell so you don't miss a single one

